.TH LUXAFOR-CALLWATCH 1 "" "luxafor-status" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luxafor-callwatch \- switch the Luxafor light to a status during calls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luxafor-callwatch
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luxafor-callwatch
watches which applications record from the microphone, through
.BR pactl (1)
(PipeWire or PulseAudio). When a watched application \(em a web browser by
default, which covers Teams, Odoo, Google Meet, Jitsi and other calls in a
browser tab \(em starts recording, the light switches to the call status.
When the call ends, the previous status comes back, unless the status was
changed by hand during the call.
.PP
It is started at login through
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart/luxafor-callwatch.desktop .
.PP
Only one runs per user: a second one leaves right away.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Show the applications using the microphone right now, and whether that
counts as a call. Run it during a call to check the detection.
.PP
A timer set with
.B luxafor-toggle \-\-for
keeps running during a call. If it ends during the call, the light goes to
the default status when the call ends.
.SH CONFIGURATION
In
.I ~/.config/luxafor-status/statuses.conf
(Luxafor Panel \(-> Settings, or see
.BR luxafor-toggle (1)),
read at each call:
.TP
.B call-status
Status used during calls (default:
.BR call );
.B none
turns call detection off.
.TP
.B call-apps
Space-separated names matched against the application name and binary
(default: common web browsers).
.PP
.I ~/.config/luxafor-status/callwatch.conf
is no longer read since 1.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR luxafor-toggle (1),
.BR luxafor-tray (1),
.BR pactl (1)
